}
Ahí React solo necesita:

payload.params → para knobs host/automation (APVTS mirror).
​

payload.preset.layers[0].voiceArchitecture → para panel ACE “profundo”.
​

¿Te va bien si el siguiente paso es definir exactamente qué campos meterías en un state “lite” (sin toda la voiceArchitecture) para vistas tipo browser/lista de presets?



Para un “state lite” de browser lo ideal es exponer solo lo necesario para listar y filtrar presets, sin voiceArchitecture ni rutas de modulación.
​

1. Forma del state lite
Ejemplo de payload que podría devolver getState cuando el modo es “browser”:

text
{
  "type": "state",
  "requestId": "req-browser-1",
  "payload": {
    "mode": "browser",
    "currentPresetId": "ACE-JUNO-BASIC-PAD",
    "presets": [
      {
        "id": "ACE-JUNO-BASIC-PAD",
        "name": "ACE Juno Basic Pad",
        "author": "abdeneurolab",
        "engine": "VirtualAnalog",
        "tags": ["pad", "juno", "warm", "chorus"],
        "bpm": 128,
        "key": "C minor",
        "layersSummary": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "name": "Juno Basic",
            "engine": "VirtualAnalog",
            "polyphony": 8,
            "hasChorus": true,
            "category": "pad"
          }
        ],
        "rating": null,
        "favorite": false
      },
      {
        "id": "HYBRID-MS20-JP-PAD",
        "name": "Hybrid MS20 JP Supersaw",
        "author": "abdeneurolab",
        "engine": "VirtualAnalog",
        "tags": ["pad", "hybrid", "ms20", "jp8000"],
        "bpm": 132,
        "key": "D minor",
        "layersSummary": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "name": "MS20 Grit",
            "engine": "VirtualAnalog",
            "polyphony": 8,
            "hasChorus": false,
            "category": "bass-pad"
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "name": "JP Supersaw Pad",
            "engine": "VirtualAnalog",
            "polyphony": 8,
            "hasChorus": true,
            "category": "pad"
          }
        ],
        "rating": 4.5,
        "favorite": true
      }
    ]
  }
}
Campos clave:

id, name, author, engine → identifican claramente el preset.
​

tags, bpm, key → para filtros rápidos en el browser.
​

layersSummary → solo un resumen por capa (nombre, polyphony, algún flag práctico como hasChorus).
​

Campos “sociales” opcionales (rating, favorite) ya preparados para futuro.

2. JSON completo vs lite
Con esto puedes:

Usar state completo (con preset.voiceArchitecture) solo al abrir el editor de detalle.

Usar state lite (lista de presets) para el browser, sin cargar todo el grafo ACE ni diffs.

¿Te interesa que te proponga también los mensajes JSON mínimos para paginar y filtrar el browser (listPresets, filterPresets, loadPresetFromBrowser)?


Definimos tres mensajes nuevos para el browser, apoyados en el esquema y protocolo que ya tienes.

Mensajes UI → Core
listPresets
Lista presets con paginación y filtros simples.

text
{
  "type": "listPresets",
  "requestId": "req-list-1",
  "payload": {
    "offset": 0,
    "limit": 50,
    "filters": {
      "engine": "VirtualAnalog",      // opcional
      "tags": ["pad", "juno"],        // AND lógico
      "text": "supersaw",             // búsqueda por nombre/autor/tags
      "favorite": true,               // opcional
      "bankId": "ROLAND-VA"           // opcional, para bancos/carpetas
    },
    "sort": {
      "field": "name",                // name | author | bpm | lastModified
      "direction": "asc"              // asc | desc
    }
  }
}
loadPresetFromBrowser
Selecciona un preset de la lista y lo carga (igual que loadPreset, pero explícito desde el browser).
​

text
{
  "type": "loadPresetFromBrowser",
  "requestId": "req-load-1",
  "payload": {
    "presetId": "ACE-JUNO-BASIC-PAD"
  }
}
filterPresets (opcional en v1)
Para cambiar solo filtros sin redefinir paginación.
​

text
{
  "type": "filterPresets",
  "requestId": "req-filter-1",
  "payload": {
    "filters": {
      "tags": ["ms20"],
      "engine": "VirtualAnalog"
    }
  }
}
Mensajes Core → UI
presets (respuesta a listPresets / filterPresets)
Usa el state lite que definimos.
​

text
{
  "type": "presets",
  "requestId": "req-list-1",
  "payload": {
    "total": 123,
    "offset": 0,
    "limit": 50,
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "ACE-JUNO-BASIC-PAD",
        "name": "ACE Juno Basic Pad",
        "author": "abdeneurolab",
        "engine": "VirtualAnalog",
        "tags": ["pad", "juno", "warm", "chorus"],
        "bpm": 128,
        "key": "C minor",
        "bankId": "ROLAND-VA",
        "layersSummary": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "name": "Juno Basic",
            "engine": "VirtualAnalog",
            "polyphony": 8,
            "hasChorus": true,
            "category": "pad"
          }
        ],
        "rating": null,
        "favorite": false,
        "lastModified": "2026-03-17T10:33:00Z"
      }
    ]
  }
}
presetChanged (ya lo usas)
Cuando loadPresetFromBrowser aplica y el engine cambia de snapshot, puedes seguir emitiendo:

text
{
  "type": "presetChanged",
  "payload": {
    "presetId": "ACE-JUNO-BASIC-PAD",
    "name": "ACE Juno Basic Pad"
  }
}
Con esto, el browser puede:

Llamar a listPresets al montar.

Repetir listPresets o filterPresets al cambiar filtros/página.

Llamar a loadPresetFromBrowser al hacer clic, y actualizar la UI con presetChanged + state completo.
​

¿Quieres que el siguiente paso sea esquematizar el repositorio de presets en C++ (PresetRepository) que implementa internamente listPresets con estos filtros?


Te propongo ir al grano con la interfaz mínima de PresetRepository en C++ que implemente justo esos mensajes listPresets / loadPresetFromBrowser.

Interfaz mínima de PresetRepository
cpp
// OmegaCore/Preset/PresetRepository.h
#pragma once
#include <functional>
#include <vector>
#include <optional>
#include <string>

namespace Omega::Preset
{
    struct PresetSummary
    {
        std::string id;              // "ACE-JUNO-BASIC-PAD"
        std::string name;
        std::string author;
        std::string engine;          // "VirtualAnalog"
        std::vector<std::string> tags;
        int bpm = 0;
        std::string key;             // "C minor"
        std::string bankId;          // "ROLAND-VA"
        struct LayerSummary {
            std::string id;          // "A"
            std::string name;        // "Juno Basic"
            std::string engine;
            int polyphony = 8;
            bool hasChorus = false;
            std::string category;    // "pad", "bass"...
        };
        std::vector<LayerSummary> layers;
        bool favorite = false;
        double lastModifiedUnix = 0.0; // o ISO8601 en string si prefieres
    };

    struct ListFilters
    {
        std::optional<std::string> engine;
        std::vector<std::string> tags;      // AND
        std::optional<std::string> text;    // name/author/tags contiene
        std::optional<bool> favorite;
        std::optional<std::string> bankId;
    };

    enum class SortField { Name, Author, Bpm, LastModified };
    enum class SortDirection { Asc, Desc };

    struct ListRequest
    {
        int offset = 0;
        int limit  = 50;
        ListFilters filters;
        SortField sortField = SortField::Name;
        SortDirection sortDirection = SortDirection::Asc;
    };

    struct ListResult
    {
        int total = 0;
        int offset = 0;
        int limit  = 0;
        std::vector<PresetSummary> items;
    };

    class PresetRepository
    {
    public:
        virtual ~PresetRepository() = default;

        // Carga inicial desde disco / recursos
        virtual void reload() = 0;

        // Para listPresets / filterPresets
        virtual ListResult listPresets(const ListRequest& request) const = 0;

        // Para loadPresetFromBrowser / loadPreset
        // Devuelve el ValueTree/Blob bruto del preset para pasarlo a OmegaPreset/AceValidator
        virtual bool loadPresetData(const std::string& presetId,
                                    std::string& outSerializedPreset) const = 0;

        // Marcar favorito (para que el browser pueda togglear)
        virtual bool setFavorite(const std::string& presetId, bool favorite) = 0;
    };
}
Con esto puedes:

Implementar PresetRepositoryFilesystem o PresetRepositoryResources detrás.

Mapear 1:1 los JSON de listPresets ↔ ListRequest / ListResult, y loadPresetFromBrowser ↔ loadPresetData + pipeline OmegaPreset + AceValidator + EngineConfig.
​

¿Te apetece que el siguiente paso sea dibujar el adaptador C++ que convierte el JSON listPresets del OmegaUiBridge en un ListRequest y devuelve presets al Web UI?

Te dejo el adaptador C++ lo más directo posible entre OmegaUiBridge y PresetRepository para listPresets / presets.

Manejo de listPresets en OmegaUiBridge
cpp
// OmegaUiBridge.h
#include "PresetRepository.h"

class OmegaUiBridge
{
public:
    OmegaUiBridge(Omega::Preset::PresetRepository& repo,
                  juce::AudioProcessorValueTreeState& apvts)
        : mRepo(repo), mApvts(apvts) {}

    void handleMessageFromUi(const juce::String& jsonText);

    std::function<void(const juce::String&)> sendToUi;

private:
    void handleListPresets(const juce::var& msg);
    juce::String buildPresetsJson(const juce::String& requestId,
                                  const Omega::Preset::ListResult& result);

    Omega::Preset::PresetRepository& mRepo;
    juce::AudioProcessorValueTreeState& mApvts;
};
cpp
// OmegaUiBridge.cpp
void OmegaUiBridge::handleMessageFromUi(const juce::String& jsonText)
{
    juce::var msg = juce::JSON::parse(jsonText);
    if (!msg.isObject())
        return;

    auto* obj = msg.getDynamicObject();
    auto type      = obj->getProperty("type").toString();
    auto requestId = obj->getProperty("requestId").toString();

    if (type == "listPresets")
    {
        handleListPresets(msg);
    }
    else if (type == "loadPresetFromBrowser")
    {
        // aquí llamas a tu pipeline existente loadPreset(presetId) + buildStateJson
        auto* payload = obj->getProperty("payload").getDynamicObject();
        if (!payload) return;
        auto presetId = payload->getProperty("presetId").toString();

        // loadPresetData + OmegaPreset + AceValidator + EngineConfig...
        // ...

        if (sendToUi)
        {
            // opcional: responder con state + presetChanged
        }
    }
    // resto: getState, setParam, loadPreset, savePreset, listAceComponents...
}
Parsear listPresets → ListRequest
cpp
void OmegaUiBridge::handleListPresets(const juce::var& msg)
{
    auto* obj = msg.getDynamicObject();
    if (!obj) return;

    auto requestId = obj->getProperty("requestId").toString();
    auto payload   = obj->getProperty("payload");

    Omega::Preset::ListRequest req;

    if (auto* p = payload.getDynamicObject())
    {
        // offset / limit
        req.offset = int(p->getProperty("offset", 0));
        req.limit  = int(p->getProperty("limit", 50));

        // filters
        auto filtersVar = p->getProperty("filters");
        if (auto* f = filtersVar.getDynamicObject())
        {
            auto engine = f->getProperty("engine").toString();
            if (engine.isNotEmpty())
                req.filters.engine = engine.toStdString();

            auto text = f->getProperty("text").toString();
            if (text.isNotEmpty())
                req.filters.text = text.toStdString();

            if (!f->getProperty("favorite").isVoid())
                req.filters.favorite = bool(f->getProperty("favorite"));

            auto bankId = f->getProperty("bankId").toString();
            if (bankId.isNotEmpty())
                req.filters.bankId = bankId.toStdString();

            auto tagsVar = f->getProperty("tags");
            if (tagsVar.isArray())
            {
                auto* arr = tagsVar.getArray();
                for (auto& v : *arr)
                    req.filters.tags.push_back(v.toString().toStdString());
            }
        }

        // sort
        auto sortVar = p->getProperty("sort");
        if (auto* s = sortVar.getDynamicObject())
        {
            auto field = s->getProperty("field").toString();
            if (field == "author")       req.sortField = Omega::Preset::SortField::Author;
            else if (field == "bpm")     req.sortField = Omega::Preset::SortField::Bpm;
            else if (field == "lastModified")
                req.sortField = Omega::Preset::SortField::LastModified;
            else                         req.sortField = Omega::Preset::SortField::Name;

            auto dir = s->getProperty("direction").toString();
            req.sortDirection = (dir == "desc")
                ? Omega::Preset::SortDirection::Desc
                : Omega::Preset::SortDirection::Asc;
        }
    }

    auto result = mRepo.listPresets(req);

    if (sendToUi)
        sendToUi(buildPresetsJson(requestId, result));
}
ListResult → mensaje presets
cpp
juce::String OmegaUiBridge::buildPresetsJson(
    const juce::String& requestId,
    const Omega::Preset::ListResult& result)
{
    juce::DynamicObject::Ptr root   = new juce::DynamicObject();
    juce::DynamicObject::Ptr payload = new juce::DynamicObject();

    root->setProperty("type", "presets");
    root->setProperty("requestId", requestId);

    payload->setProperty("total",  result.total);
    payload->setProperty("offset", result.offset);
    payload->setProperty("limit",  result.limit);

    juce::Array<juce::var> itemsArray;

    for (const auto& p : result.items)
    {
        juce::DynamicObject::Ptr item = new juce::DynamicObject();
        item->setProperty("id",      p.id);
        item->setProperty("name",    p.name);
        item->setProperty("author",  p.author);
        item->setProperty("engine",  p.engine);
        item->setProperty("bpm",     p.bpm);
        item->setProperty("key",     p.key);
        item->setProperty("bankId",  p.bankId);
        item->setProperty("favorite", p.favorite);
        item->setProperty("lastModified", p.lastModifiedUnix); // o ISO string

        // tags
        juce::Array<juce::var> tags;
        for (auto& t : p.tags)
            tags.add(juce::String(t));
        item->setProperty("tags", tags);

        // layersSummary
        juce::Array<juce::var> layers;
        for (auto& l : p.layers)
        {
            juce::DynamicObject::Ptr lobj = new juce::DynamicObject();
            lobj->setProperty("id",        l.id);
            lobj->setProperty("name",      l.name);
            lobj->setProperty("engine",    l.engine);
            lobj->setProperty("polyphony", l.polyphony);
            lobj->setProperty("hasChorus", l.hasChorus);
            lobj->setProperty("category",  l.category);
            layers.add(juce::var(lobj.get()));
        }
        item->setProperty("layersSummary", layers);

        itemsArray.add(juce::var(item.get()));
    }

    payload->setProperty("items", itemsArray);
    root->setProperty("payload", juce::var(payload.get()));

    return juce::JSON::toString(juce::var(root.get()));
}
Con esto, el browser React solo necesita mandar type: "listPresets" y leer type: "presets" para popular la tabla.
​

¿Te gustaría que el siguiente paso sea esbozar el hook React usePresetBrowser que mande listPresets y reciba presets sobre window.OmegaCore?


Te hago el hook usePresetBrowser completo y el shape de estado, listo para pegar.

Shape de estado
ts
// usePresetBrowser.ts
export type PresetListItem = {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  author: string;
  engine: string;
  bpm: number | null;
  key: string | null;
  bankId: string | null;
  favorite: boolean;
  lastModified: number; // unix o ms, según envíes
  tags: string[];
  layersSummary: {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    engine: string;
    polyphony: number;
    hasChorus: boolean;
    category: string | null;
  }[];
};

export type PresetFilters = {
  text?: string;
  engine?: string;
  favorite?: boolean;
  bankId?: string;
  tags?: string[];
};

export type PresetSortField = 'name' | 'author' | 'bpm' | 'lastModified';
export type SortDirection = 'asc' | 'desc';

export type PresetSort = {
  field: PresetSortField;
  direction: SortDirection;
};

export type UsePresetBrowserState = {
  items: PresetListItem[];
  total: number;
  offset: number;
  limit: number;
  loading: boolean;
  error: string | null;
  filters: PresetFilters;
  sort: PresetSort;
};
Hook usePresetBrowser
ts
// usePresetBrowser.ts
import { useCallback, useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';

type OmegaCoreBridge = {
  sendMessage?: (msg: any) => void;
  onMessage?: (handler: (jsonText: string) => void) => void;
};

declare global {
  interface Window {
    OmegaCore?: OmegaCoreBridge;
  }
}

export type {
  PresetListItem,
  PresetFilters,
  PresetSort,
  UsePresetBrowserState,
};

function makeRequestId(prefix: string) {
  return `${prefix}-${Date.now()}-${Math.floor(Math.random() * 1e6)}`;
}

export function usePresetBrowser(initialLimit = 50) {
  const [state, setState] = useState<UsePresetBrowserState>({
    items: [],
    total: 0,
    offset: 0,
    limit: initialLimit,
    loading: false,
    error: null,
    filters: {},
    sort: { field: 'name', direction: 'asc' },
  });

  const pendingRequestId = useRef<string | null>(null);

  const sendMessage = useCallback((msg: any) => {
    if (window.OmegaCore && typeof window.OmegaCore.sendMessage === 'function') {
      window.OmegaCore.sendMessage(msg);
    } else {
      // dev fallback
      // console.warn('OmegaCore.sendMessage not available', msg);
    }
  }, []);

  const requestPage = useCallback(
    (opts?: {
      offset?: number;
      limit?: number;
      filters?: PresetFilters;
      sort?: PresetSort;
    }) => {
      const offset = opts?.offset ?? state.offset;
      const limit = opts?.limit ?? state.limit;
      const filters = opts?.filters ?? state.filters;
      const sort = opts?.sort ?? state.sort;

      const reqId = makeRequestId('listPresets');
      pendingRequestId.current = reqId;

      setState((prev) => ({
        ...prev,
        loading: true,
        error: null,
        offset,
        limit,
        filters,
        sort,
      }));

      sendMessage({
        type: 'listPresets',
        requestId: reqId,
        payload: {
          offset,
          limit,
          filters,
          sort,
        },
      });
    },
    [sendMessage, state.offset, state.limit, state.filters, state.sort],
  );

  const applyFilters = useCallback(
    (filters: PresetFilters) => {
      // reset a primera página
      requestPage({ offset: 0, filters });
    },
    [requestPage],
  );

  const setSort = useCallback(
    (sort: PresetSort) => {
      requestPage({ offset: 0, sort });
    },
    [requestPage],
  );

  const setPage = useCallback(
    (offset: number) => {
      requestPage({ offset });
    },
    [requestPage],
  );

  const reload = useCallback(() => {
    requestPage({});
  }, [requestPage]);

  useEffect(() => {
    const handleMessage = (jsonText: string) => {
      let msg: any;
      try {
        msg = JSON.parse(jsonText);
      } catch {
        return;
      }

      if (msg.type !== 'presets') return;

      const requestId: string | undefined = msg.requestId;
      if (!requestId || requestId !== pendingRequestId.current) {
        // respuesta de una página antigua: ignorar
        return;
      }

      const p = msg.payload;
      if (!p) return;

      const items: PresetListItem[] = (p.items || []).map((raw: any) => ({
        id: String(raw.id ?? ''),
        name: String(raw.name ?? ''),
        author: String(raw.author ?? ''),
        engine: String(raw.engine ?? ''),
        bpm: raw.bpm ?? null,
        key: raw.key ?? null,
        bankId: raw.bankId ?? null,
        favorite: Boolean(raw.favorite),
        lastModified: Number(raw.lastModified ?? 0),
        tags: Array.isArray(raw.tags) ? raw.tags.map((t: any) => String(t)) : [],
        layersSummary: Array.isArray(raw.layersSummary)
          ? raw.layersSummary.map((l: any) => ({
              id: String(l.id ?? ''),
              name: String(l.name ?? ''),
              engine: String(l.engine ?? ''),
              polyphony: Number(l.polyphony ?? 0),
              hasChorus: Boolean(l.hasChorus),
              category: l.category ?? null,
            }))
          : [],
      }));

      setState((prev) => ({
        ...prev,
        loading: false,
        error: null,
        items,
        total: Number(p.total ?? items.length),
        offset: Number(p.offset ?? prev.offset),
        limit: Number(p.limit ?? prev.limit),
      }));
    };

    if (!window.OmegaCore) {
      (window as any).OmegaCore = {};
    }

    // Registrar handler; si ya hay uno, lo envolvemos
    const existing = window.OmegaCore!.onMessage;
    if (existing) {
      window.OmegaCore!.onMessage = (jsonText: string) => {
        existing(jsonText);
        handleMessage(jsonText);
      };
    } else {
      window.OmegaCore!.onMessage = handleMessage;
    }

    // primera carga
    requestPage({ offset: 0 });

    return () => {
      // no limpiamos onMessage global aquí para no romper otros hooks;
      // en un sistema real usarías un bus de eventos propio.
    };
  }, [requestPage]);

  return {
    state,
    items: state.items,
    total: state.total,
    offset: state.offset,
    limit: state.limit,
    loading: state.loading,
    error: state.error,
    filters: state.filters,
    sort: state.sort,
    setPage,
    applyFilters,
    setSort,
    reload,
  };
}
Este hook asume exactamente el contrato listPresets / presets que cableaste en OmegaUiBridge en el mensaje anterior.
​

¿Quieres que te haga ahora mismo un componente <PresetTable /> en React que use este hook y soporte paginación y clic para loadPresetFromBrowser?


Te dejo un <PresetTable /> mínimo con paginación y doble clic para loadPresetFromBrowser, usando usePresetBrowser y el contrato JSON que definimos.
​

Componente PresetTable básico
tsx
// PresetTable.tsx
import React, { useCallback } from 'react';
import {
  usePresetBrowser,
  PresetListItem,
} from './usePresetBrowser';

type OmegaCoreBridge = {
  sendMessage?: (msg: any) => void;
};

declare global {
  interface Window {
    OmegaCore?: OmegaCoreBridge;
  }
}

function sendLoadPresetFromBrowser(id: string) {
  if (!window.OmegaCore || typeof window.OmegaCore.sendMessage !== 'function') {
    // console.warn('OmegaCore.sendMessage not available for loadPresetFromBrowser');
    return;
  }

  window.OmegaCore.sendMessage({
    type: 'loadPresetFromBrowser',
    requestId: `loadPresetFromBrowser-${Date.now()}-${Math.floor(Math.random() * 1e6)}`,
    payload: { presetId: id },
  });
}

export const PresetTable: React.FC = () => {
  const {
    items,
    total,
    offset,
    limit,
    loading,
    error,
    setPage,
  } = usePresetBrowser(25);

  const currentPage = Math.floor(offset / limit) + 1;
  const totalPages = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(total / limit));

  const handleRowDoubleClick = useCallback((preset: PresetListItem) => {
    sendLoadPresetFromBrowser(preset.id);
  }, []);

  const handlePrevPage = useCallback(() => {
    const newOffset = Math.max(0, offset - limit);
    setPage(newOffset);
  }, [offset, limit, setPage]);

  const handleNextPage = useCallback(() => {
    const newOffset = Math.min(total - limit, offset + limit);
    setPage(Math.max(0, newOffset));
  }, [offset, limit, total, setPage]);

  return (
    <div className="preset-table">
      <div className="preset-table-header">
        <h2>Presets</h2>
        <div className="preset-table-meta">
          <span>
            {loading ? 'Loading…' : `${total} presets`}
          </span>
          {error && <span className="preset-table-error">{error}</span>}
        </div>
      </div>

      <table className="preset-table-grid">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Author</th>
            <th>Engine</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {items.length === 0 && !loading && (
            <tr>
              <td colSpan={3} style={{ textAlign: 'center', opacity: 0.7 }}>
                No presets found
              </td>
            </tr>
          )}

          {items.map((preset) => (
            <tr
              key={preset.id}
              onDoubleClick={() => handleRowDoubleClick(preset)}
              style={{ cursor: 'pointer' }}
            >
              <td>{preset.name}</td>
              <td>{preset.author}</td>
              <td>{preset.engine}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div className="preset-table-footer">
        <button
          type="button"
          onClick={handlePrevPage}
          disabled={loading || currentPage <= 1}
        >
          ‹ Prev
        </button>
        <span>
          Page {currentPage} / {totalPages}
        </span>
        <button
          type="button"
          onClick={handleNextPage}
          disabled={loading || currentPage >= totalPages}
        >
          Next ›
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};
Resumen columnas actuales
Columna	Fuente JSON	Comentario
Name	item.name	Doble clic lanza loadPresetFromBrowser
Author	item.author	Solo lectura de momento
Engine	item.engine	VirtualAnalog, etc.
¿Te apetece que el siguiente paso sea añadir filtros rápidos por texto y engine encima de esta tabla (input + select) usando applyFilters del hook?


Te añado filtro de texto y un indicador visual del preset cargado actual, manteniendo la tabla simple.
​

Hook extendido: presetId actual
Primero, un mini hook para escuchar presetChanged y saber qué preset está cargado:

ts
// useCurrentPresetId.ts
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';

type OmegaCoreBridge = {
  onMessage?: (handler: (jsonText: string) => void) => void;
};

declare global {
  interface Window {
    OmegaCore?: OmegaCoreBridge;
  }
}

export function useCurrentPresetId() {
  const [currentPresetId, setCurrentPresetId] = useState<string | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const handleMessage = (jsonText: string) => {
      let msg: any;
      try {
        msg = JSON.parse(jsonText);
      } catch {
        return;
      }

      if (msg.type === 'presetChanged' && msg.payload?.presetId) {
        setCurrentPresetId(String(msg.payload.presetId));
      }

      if (msg.type === 'state' && msg.payload?.preset?.id) {
        // también puedes inicializar desde state completo
        setCurrentPresetId(String(msg.payload.preset.id));
      }
    };

    if (!window.OmegaCore) {
      (window as any).OmegaCore = {};
    }

    const existing = window.OmegaCore!.onMessage;
    if (existing) {
      window.OmegaCore!.onMessage = (jsonText: string) => {
        existing(jsonText);
        handleMessage(jsonText);
      };
    } else {
      window.OmegaCore!.onMessage = handleMessage;
    }

    return () => {
      // mismo comentario que antes: no desmontamos el global aquí
    };
  }, []);

  return currentPresetId;
}
Esto asume que ya emites presetChanged y state desde OmegaUiBridge como definimos.
​

PresetTable con filtro de texto + highlight
tsx
// PresetTable.tsx
import React, { useCallback, useState } from 'react';
import {
  usePresetBrowser,
  PresetListItem,
} from './usePresetBrowser';
import { useCurrentPresetId } from './useCurrentPresetId';

type OmegaCoreBridge = {
  sendMessage?: (msg: any) => void;
};

declare global {
  interface Window {
    OmegaCore?: OmegaCoreBridge;
  }
}

function sendLoadPresetFromBrowser(id: string) {
  if (!window.OmegaCore || typeof window.OmegaCore.sendMessage !== 'function') {
    return;
  }

  window.OmegaCore.sendMessage({
    type: 'loadPresetFromBrowser',
    requestId: `loadPresetFromBrowser-${Date.now()}-${Math.floor(
      Math.random() * 1e6,
    )}`,
    payload: { presetId: id },
  });
}

export const PresetTable: React.FC = () => {
  const {
    items,
    total,
    offset,
    limit,
    loading,
    error,
    setPage,
    applyFilters,
    state,
  } = usePresetBrowser(25);
  const currentPresetId = useCurrentPresetId();

  const [textFilter, setTextFilter] = useState(state.filters.text ?? '');

  const currentPage = Math.floor(offset / limit) + 1;
  const totalPages = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(total / limit));

  const handleRowDoubleClick = useCallback((preset: PresetListItem) => {
    sendLoadPresetFromBrowser(preset.id);
  }, []);

  const handlePrevPage = useCallback(() => {
    const newOffset = Math.max(0, offset - limit);
    setPage(newOffset);
  }, [offset, limit, setPage]);

  const handleNextPage = useCallback(() => {
    const newOffset = Math.min(Math.max(0, total - limit), offset + limit);
    setPage(newOffset);
  }, [offset, limit, total, setPage]);

  const handleTextFilterChange = useCallback(
    (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {
      const value = e.target.value;
      setTextFilter(value);
      applyFilters({
        ...state.filters,
        text: value || undefined,
      });
    },
    [applyFilters, state.filters],
  );

  return (
    <div className="preset-table">
      <div className="preset-table-header">
        <h2>Presets</h2>
        <div className="preset-table-meta">
          <input
            type="text"
            placeholder="Search presets…"
            value={textFilter}
            onChange={handleTextFilterChange}
            style={{ minWidth: 180 }}
          />
          <span>
            {loading ? 'Loading…' : `${total} presets`}
          </span>
          {error && <span className="preset-table-error">{error}</span>}
        </div>
      </div>

      <table className="preset-table-grid">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Loaded</th>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Author</th>
            <th>Engine</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {items.length === 0 && !loading && (
            <tr>
              <td colSpan={4} style={{ textAlign: 'center', opacity: 0.7 }}>
                No presets found
              </td>
            </tr>
          )}

          {items.map((preset) => {
            const isCurrent = currentPresetId === preset.id;
            return (
              <tr
                key={preset.id}
                onDoubleClick={() => handleRowDoubleClick(preset)}
                className={isCurrent ? 'preset-row-current' : undefined}
                style={{
                  cursor: 'pointer',
                  backgroundColor: isCurrent ? 'rgba(0, 200, 255, 0.12)' : undefined,
                }}
              >
                <td style={{ textAlign: 'center' }}>
                  {isCurrent ? '●' : ''}
                </td>
                <td>{preset.name}</td>
                <td>{preset.author}</td>
                <td>{preset.engine}</td>
              </tr>
            );
          })}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div className="preset-table-footer">
        <button
          type="button"
          onClick={handlePrevPage}
          disabled={loading || currentPage <= 1}
        >
          ‹ Prev
        </button>
        <span>
          Page {currentPage} / {totalPages}
        </span>
        <button
          type="button"
          onClick={handleNextPage}
          disabled={loading || currentPage >= totalPages}
        >
          Next ›
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};
Esto te deja ya:

Filtro de texto que viaja como filters.text en listPresets.

Doble clic que manda loadPresetFromBrowser.

Indicador de preset actual con “●” y fila resaltada cuando llega presetChanged o state.
