Dos detalles pequeños pero muy útiles para este MVP:

Añadir un “preset de diagnóstico” silencioso

Un YAML que deja el DCO, filtro y env en valores neutros (por ejemplo, cutoff alto, env sustain=1, release corto).

Sirve para comprobar rápidamente que el flujo MIDI/engine/WebUI funciona aunque el DSP real todavía sea simple.
​

Un parámetro APVTS ENGINEBYPASS

Mapeado a un toggle en la WebUI y al editor JUCE de emergencia.

Te permite comparar fácilmente “señal seca del host” vs “engine VA” y detectar si los clicks o artefactos vienen del motor o de otra parte de la cadena.
​

¿Quieres que te proponga el YAML exacto de ese preset de diagnóstico silencioso (o casi) para testear el flujo sin preocuparte aún del sonido final?


Preset de diagnóstico muy simple, sin movimiento en filtro ni modulación, pensado para verificar flujo sin que el sonido te distraiga.
​

text
omegapresetversion: 1
name: "Diag - Static Saw"
author: "abdeneurolab"
engine: "VirtualAnalog"

layers:
  - id: "A"
    name: "Diag Saw"
    polyphony: 8

    voicearchitecture:
      oscillators:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "OSC-VA-001"   # Juno DCO
          enabled: true
          params:
            tune: 0.0
            pulsewidth: 0.5
            sublevel: 0.0

      filters:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "FLT-VA-001"   # IR3109 LP24
          enabled: true
          mode: "LP24"
          params:
            cutoff: 20000.0           # filtro totalmente abierto
            resonance: 0.0
            drive: 0.0

      envelopes:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "ENV-ADSR-GEN"
          role: "amp"
          params:
            attack: 5.0               # ataque rápido pero no click
            decay: 0.0
            sustain: 1.0              # nivel constante
            release: 80.0             # release corto para oír note-off

      lfos:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "LFO-001"
          enabled: false              # LFO desactivado

      fx:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "FX-CH-001"
          enabled: false              # chorus desactivado

    modulationroutes: []              # sin modulación

    layerparams:
      leveldb: 0.0
      pan: 0.0
      mute: false
Osc: saw estática sin sub ni PWM ni LFO.
​

Filtro: corte al máximo, sin env, sin LFO, sin keytrack ni nada que mueva el timbre.
​

Amp env: ataque corto, sustain 1, release corto: ideal para oír claramente Note On/Off y All Notes Off.

Sin chorus ni mod routes: cualquier movimiento que escuches viene de bugs, no de modulación.

¿Quieres que te sugiera también un “Init Pad” muy cercano a tu “ACE Juno Basic Pad” pero más neutro (cutoff medio, un poco de env al filtro, LFO lento) como siguiente punto de comparación audible?


Aquí tienes un “Init Pad” tipo Juno, neutro pero ya útil para oír movimiento sin volverte loco afinando carácter.
​

text
omegapresetversion: 1
name: "Init Juno Pad"
author: "abdeneurolab"
engine: "VirtualAnalog"

layers:
  - id: "A"
    name: "Init Pad"
    polyphony: 8

    voicearchitecture:
      oscillators:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "OSC-VA-001"     # DCO Juno-like
          enabled: true
          params:
            waveform: "SAW"            # solo saw, clásico pad Juno[web:287]
            mixsquare: 0.0
            sublevel: 0.2
            tune: 0.0
            detune: 0.0

      filters:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "FLT-VA-001"
          enabled: true
          mode: "LP24"
          params:
            cutoff: 3500.0             # algo cerrado, pad suave[web:287]
            resonance: 0.15
            envamount: 0.35            # ligera apertura con el env
            keytrack: 0.4
            drive: 0.0

      envelopes:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "ENV-ADSR-GEN"
          role: "amp"
          params:
            attack: 120.0              # ataque lento tipo pad[web:290]
            decay: 60.0
            sustain: 0.8
            release: 140.0

        - slot: 2
          componentid: "ENV-ADSR-GEN"
          role: "filter"
          params:
            attack: 90.0               # abre un poco el filtro
            decay: 120.0
            sustain: 0.4
            release: 160.0

      lfos:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "LFO-001"
          enabled: true
          params:
            ratehz: 0.35              # LFO lento
            waveform: "TRI"
            fadeinms: 800.0
            amount_pitch: 0.02        # vibrato muy sutil[web:287]
            amount_pwm: 0.1
            amount_filter: 0.0

      fx:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "FX-CH-001"
          enabled: true
          params:
            ratehz: 0.25
            depth: 0.4
            mix: 0.35                  # chorus moderado, no “mega Juno” aún[web:287]

    modulationroutes:
      - source: "LFO1"
        destination: "DCO_PITCH"
        amount: 0.02
      - source: "LFO1"
        destination: "DCO_PWM"
        amount: 0.1
      - source: "ENV_FILTER"
        destination: "VCF_CUTOFF"
        amount: 0.35

    layerparams:
      leveldb: -3.0
      pan: 0.0
      mute: false
Con esto ya tienes tres escalones de test: engine bypass → Diag Static Saw → Init Juno Pad (básico pero musical).

Si tu engine aún no soporta alguno de estos campos (waveform, amount_pwm, etc.), los quitamos o los simplificamos a lo que tengas implementado ahora y mantenemos el “shape” general.

¿En tu LayerASettings actual qué subset de parámetros está ya cableado (waveform, envamount, LFO→pitch/PWM, chorus), para ajustarlo exactamente a lo que puedes mapear hoy?



Te añado solo dos piezas que completan el “preset kit” inicial para tu MVP VA/ACE.
​

1. Preset Juno básico definitivo
Úsalo como “happy path” canónico para todo el vertical VA‑ACE (carga → AceValidator → VoiceFactory → EngineConfig → audio).
​

text
omegapresetversion: 1
name: "ACE Juno Basic Pad"
author: "abdeneurolab"
engine: "VirtualAnalog"

global:
  mastergaindb: 0.0

layers:
  - id: "A"
    name: "Juno Basic"
    engine: "VirtualAnalog"
    polyphony: 8

    layerparams:
      leveldb: 0.0
      pan: 0.0
      maincutoffhz: 2000.0      # LAYERAMAINCUTOFF
      mainresonance: 0.2        # LAYERAMAINRES
      envamount: 0.5            # LAYERAENVAMT
      lforatehz: 1.0            # LAYERALFORATEHZ
      lfodepthsemis: 0.3        # LAYERALFODEPTHSEMITONES
      ampenv:
        attackms: 10.0          # LAYERAAMPATTACKMS
        decayms: 120.0          # LAYERAAMPDECAYMS
        sustain: 0.8            # LAYERAAMPSUSTAIN
        releasems: 600.0        # LAYERAAMPRELEASEMS

    voicearchitecture:
      oscillators:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "OSC-VA-001"
          enabled: true
          params:
            tune: 0.0
            pulsewidth: 0.5
            sublevel: 0.3

      filters:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "FLT-VA-001"
          enabled: true
          mode: "LP24"
          params:
            cutoff: 2000.0
            resonance: 0.2
            drive: 0.0

      envelopes:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "ENV-ADSR-GEN"
          role: "amp"
          params:
            attack: 10.0
            decay: 120.0
            sustain: 0.8
            release: 600.0

      lfos:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "LFO-001"
          params:
            rate: 1.0
            shape: "sine"
            delay: 0.0

      fx:
        - slot: 1
          componentid: "FX-CH-001"
          enabled: true
          params:
            mix: 0.7
            mode: "III"

    modulationroutes:
      - source: "LFO1"
        destination: "LayerA.Osc1.pitch"
        amount: 0.3
        curve: "sine"
        bipolar: true

      - source: "ENV1"
        destination: "LayerA.Filter1.cutoff"
        amount: 0.5
        curve: "exponential"
        bipolar: false
2. Micro‑checklist de presets para arrancar
Diag Static Saw (el silencioso/casi estático que ya te pasé).
​

ACE Juno Basic Pad (este de arriba, único objetivo: “suena sin tocar nada”).
​

Más adelante: Hybrid MS‑20 + JP Supersaw, como primer test de ACE con dos layers.
​

Con estos dos primeros ya puedes diseñar todo el pipeline pensando “solo tengo que conseguir que este YAML suene y no se rompa en ninguna capa”. ¿Te preparo ahora mismo la versión ValueTree “expandida” del ACE Juno Basic Pad tal y como la espera OmegaPreset para que puedas mapear 1:1 en código?

Aquí tienes el ACE Juno Basic Pad como juce::ValueTree exactamente en el esquema que has definido para OMEGAPRESET.
​

cpp
// OMEGAPRESET root
juce::ValueTree presetVT { "OMEGAPRESET" };
presetVT.setProperty ("schemaversion", 4, nullptr);
presetVT.setProperty ("acecatalogversion", 1, nullptr);

// metadata
{
    juce::ValueTree meta { "metadata" };
    meta.setProperty ("name",   "ACE Juno Basic Pad", nullptr);
    meta.setProperty ("author", "abdeneurolab",       nullptr);
    // created/modified/parentcommit/tags los puedes rellenar luego
    presetVT.addChild (meta, -1, nullptr);
}

// global
{
    juce::ValueTree global { "global" };
    global.setProperty ("engine",        "VirtualAnalog", nullptr);
    global.setProperty ("mastergaindb",  0.0f,            nullptr);
    global.setProperty ("masterbypass",  0,               nullptr);
    // MACRO1..4 opcionales, por ahora a 0
    global.setProperty ("MACRO1", 0.0f, nullptr);
    global.setProperty ("MACRO2", 0.0f, nullptr);
    global.setProperty ("MACRO3", 0.0f, nullptr);
    global.setProperty ("MACRO4", 0.0f, nullptr);

    presetVT.addChild (global, -1, nullptr);
}

// layers array
juce::ValueTree layersVT { "layers" };
presetVT.addChild (layersVT, -1, nullptr);

// === Layer A ===
{
    juce::ValueTree layer { "layer" };
    layer.setProperty ("id",        "A",             nullptr);
    layer.setProperty ("name",      "Juno Basic",    nullptr);
    layer.setProperty ("engine",    "VirtualAnalog", nullptr);
    layer.setProperty ("polyphony", 8,               nullptr);

    // unison (por ahora unitario)
    {
        juce::ValueTree unison { "unison" };
        unison.setProperty ("voices", 1,    nullptr);
        unison.setProperty ("detune", 0.0f, nullptr);
        unison.setProperty ("spread", 0.0f, nullptr);
        layer.addChild (unison, -1, nullptr);
    }

    // voicearchitecture
    {
        juce::ValueTree va { "voicearchitecture" };

        // oscillators
        {
            juce::ValueTree oscs { "oscillators" };

            juce::ValueTree osc { "oscillator" };
            osc.setProperty ("slot",        1,             nullptr);
            osc.setProperty ("componentid", "OSC-VA-001",  nullptr);
            osc.setProperty ("enabled",     true,          nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };

            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "tune",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "pulsewidth", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.5f,        nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "sublevel", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.3f,       nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            osc.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            oscs.addChild (osc, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (oscs, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // filters
        {
            juce::ValueTree flts { "filters" };

            juce::ValueTree flt { "filter" };
            flt.setProperty ("slot",        1,            nullptr);
            flt.setProperty ("componentid", "FLT-VA-001", nullptr);
            flt.setProperty ("enabled",     true,         nullptr);
            flt.setProperty ("mode",        "LP24",       nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };

            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "cutoff",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 2000.0f,   nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "resonance", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.2f,        nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "drive",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.0f,     nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            flt.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            flts.addChild (flt, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (flts, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // envelopes (amp)
        {
            juce::ValueTree envs { "envelopes" };

            juce::ValueTree env { "envelope" };
            env.setProperty ("slot", 1,            nullptr);
            env.setProperty ("componentid", "ENV-ADSR-GEN", nullptr);
            env.setProperty ("role", "amp",        nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };

            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "attack", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 10.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "decay",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 120.0f,   nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "sustain", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.8f,      nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "release", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 600.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            env.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            envs.addChild (env, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (envs, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // lfos
        {
            juce::ValueTree lfos { "lfos" };

            juce::ValueTree lfo { "lfo" };
            lfo.setProperty ("slot",        1,          nullptr);
            lfo.setProperty ("componentid", "LFO-001",  nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };

            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "rate",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 1.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "shape", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", "sine",  nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "delay", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            lfo.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            lfos.addChild (lfo, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (lfos, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // fx
        {
            juce::ValueTree fxs { "fx" };

            juce::ValueTree fx { "fxslot" };
            fx.setProperty ("slot",        1,            nullptr);
            fx.setProperty ("componentid", "FX-CH-001",  nullptr);
            fx.setProperty ("enabled",     true,         nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "mix",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.7f,   nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "mode", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", "III",  nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            fx.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            fxs.addChild (fx, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (fxs, -1, nullptr);
        }

        layer.addChild (va, -1, nullptr);
    }

    // modulationgraph mínimo: LFO1 → Osc1.pitch, ENV1 → Filter1.cutoff
    {
        juce::ValueTree mg { "modulationgraph" };
        mg.setProperty ("version", 1, nullptr);

        juce::ValueTree nodes { "nodes" };
        // Para MVP puedes dejar vacío y usar tus ModRoutes legacy,
        // o añadir nodos LFO/ENV si ya usas el grafo completo.
        mg.addChild (nodes, -1, nullptr);

        juce::ValueTree conns { "connections" };
        // idem: en Fase 1 puedes ignorarlo y usar modulationroutes clásicas.
        mg.addChild (conns, -1, nullptr);

        layer.addChild (mg, -1, nullptr);
    }

    // layerparams: espejo directo de los macros APVTS
    {
        juce::ValueTree lp { "layerparams" };
        lp.setProperty ("leveldb",        0.0f,   nullptr); // LAYERALEVELDB
        lp.setProperty ("pan",            0.0f,   nullptr); // LAYERAPAN
        lp.setProperty ("maincutoffhz",   2000.0f,nullptr); // LAYERAMAINCUTOFF
        lp.setProperty ("mainresonance",  0.2f,   nullptr); // LAYERAMAINRES
        lp.setProperty ("envamount",      0.5f,   nullptr); // LAYERAENVAMT
        lp.setProperty ("lforatehz",      1.0f,   nullptr); // LAYERALFORATEHZ
        lp.setProperty ("lfodepthsemis",  0.3f,   nullptr); // LAYERALFODEPTHSEMITONES

        juce::ValueTree ampEnv { "ampenv" };
        ampEnv.setProperty ("attackms",  10.0f,  nullptr);
        ampEnv.setProperty ("decayms",   120.0f, nullptr);
        ampEnv.setProperty ("sustain",   0.8f,   nullptr);
        ampEnv.setProperty ("releasems", 600.0f, nullptr);
        lp.addChild (ampEnv, -1, nullptr);

        layer.addChild (lp, -1, nullptr);
    }

    // modulationroutes “clásicas” (fuera del grafo avanzado) para Fase 1
    {
        juce::ValueTree routes { "modulationroutes" };

        {
            juce::ValueTree r { "route" };
            r.setProperty ("source",      "LFO1",                     nullptr);
            r.setProperty ("destination", "LayerA.Osc1.pitch",        nullptr);
            r.setProperty ("amount",      0.3f,                       nullptr);
            r.setProperty ("curve",       "sine",                     nullptr);
            r.setProperty ("bipolar",     true,                       nullptr);
            routes.addChild (r, -1, nullptr);
        }
        {
            juce::ValueTree r { "route" };
            r.setProperty ("source",      "ENV1",                     nullptr);
            r.setProperty ("destination", "LayerA.Filter1.cutoff",    nullptr);
            r.setProperty ("amount",      0.5f,                       nullptr);
            r.setProperty ("curve",       "exponential",              nullptr);
            r.setProperty ("bipolar",     false,                      nullptr);
            routes.addChild (r, -1, nullptr);
        }

        layer.addChild (routes, -1, nullptr);
    }

    layersVT.addChild (layer, -1, nullptr);
}
Con esto puedes:

Implementar OmegaPreset::fromValueTree y toValueTree usando este árbol como contrato.
​

Escribir un test de round‑trip que compare este ValueTree con el YAML equivalente del preset.
​

¿Quieres que el siguiente bloque sea un TestOmegaPresetJuno.cpp (Catch2) que construya exactamente este ValueTree, lo pase por OmegaPreset y verifique nombres, ids ACE y parámetros clave?

Te preparo el test de Catch2 para el preset Juno básico sobre OmegaPreset, asumiendo la API que definiste (fromValueTree, getters simples, etc.).

cpp
// Tests/TestOmegaPresetJuno.cpp
#include <catch2/catch_test_macros.hpp>
#include "Preset/OmegaPreset.h"     // tu wrapper
#include "Preset/OmegaPresetSerializer.h" // si lo usas
#include "Ace/AceCatalog.h"
#include <juce_core/juce_core.h>

using namespace OmegaPreset;
using namespace OmegaAce;

namespace
{
    juce::ValueTree createAceJunoBasicPadValueTree()
    {
        juce::ValueTree presetVT { "OMEGAPRESET" };
        presetVT.setProperty ("schemaversion", 4, nullptr);
        presetVT.setProperty ("acecatalogversion", 1, nullptr);

        // metadata
        {
            juce::ValueTree meta { "metadata" };
            meta.setProperty ("name",   "ACE Juno Basic Pad", nullptr);
            meta.setProperty ("author", "abdeneurolab",       nullptr);
            presetVT.addChild (meta, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // global
        {
            juce::ValueTree global { "global" };
            global.setProperty ("engine",       "VirtualAnalog", nullptr);
            global.setProperty ("mastergaindb", 0.0f,            nullptr);
            global.setProperty ("masterbypass", 0,               nullptr);
            global.setProperty ("MACRO1", 0.0f, nullptr);
            global.setProperty ("MACRO2", 0.0f, nullptr);
            global.setProperty ("MACRO3", 0.0f, nullptr);
            global.setProperty ("MACRO4", 0.0f, nullptr);
            presetVT.addChild (global, -1, nullptr);
        }

        juce::ValueTree layersVT { "layers" };
        presetVT.addChild (layersVT, -1, nullptr);

        juce::ValueTree layer { "layer" };
        layer.setProperty ("id",        "A",             nullptr);
        layer.setProperty ("name",      "Juno Basic",    nullptr);
        layer.setProperty ("engine",    "VirtualAnalog", nullptr);
        layer.setProperty ("polyphony", 8,               nullptr);

        // unison
        {
            juce::ValueTree unison { "unison" };
            unison.setProperty ("voices", 1,    nullptr);
            unison.setProperty ("detune", 0.0f, nullptr);
            unison.setProperty ("spread", 0.0f, nullptr);
            layer.addChild (unison, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // voicearchitecture
        juce::ValueTree va { "voicearchitecture" };

        // oscillators
        {
            juce::ValueTree oscs { "oscillators" };
            juce::ValueTree osc { "oscillator" };
            osc.setProperty ("slot",        1,             nullptr);
            osc.setProperty ("componentid", "OSC-VA-001",  nullptr);
            osc.setProperty ("enabled",     true,          nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "tune",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "pulsewidth", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.5f,        nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "sublevel", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.3f,       nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            osc.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            oscs.addChild (osc, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (oscs, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // filters
        {
            juce::ValueTree flts { "filters" };
            juce::ValueTree flt { "filter" };
            flt.setProperty ("slot",        1,            nullptr);
            flt.setProperty ("componentid", "FLT-VA-001", nullptr);
            flt.setProperty ("enabled",     true,         nullptr);
            flt.setProperty ("mode",        "LP24",       nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "cutoff",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 2000.0f,   nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "resonance", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.2f,        nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "drive",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.0f,     nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            flt.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            flts.addChild (flt, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (flts, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // envelopes
        {
            juce::ValueTree envs { "envelopes" };
            juce::ValueTree env { "envelope" };
            env.setProperty ("slot",        1,              nullptr);
            env.setProperty ("componentid", "ENV-ADSR-GEN", nullptr);
            env.setProperty ("role",        "amp",          nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "attack", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 10.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "decay",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 120.0f,   nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "sustain", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.8f,      nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "release", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 600.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            env.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            envs.addChild (env, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (envs, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // lfos
        {
            juce::ValueTree lfos { "lfos" };
            juce::ValueTree lfo { "lfo" };
            lfo.setProperty ("slot",        1,          nullptr);
            lfo.setProperty ("componentid", "LFO-001",  nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "rate",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 1.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "shape", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", "sine",  nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "delay", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.0f,    nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            lfo.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            lfos.addChild (lfo, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (lfos, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // fx
        {
            juce::ValueTree fxs { "fx" };
            juce::ValueTree fx { "fxslot" };
            fx.setProperty ("slot",        1,            nullptr);
            fx.setProperty ("componentid", "FX-CH-001",  nullptr);
            fx.setProperty ("enabled",     true,         nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree params { "parameters" };
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "mix",  nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", 0.7f,   nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree p { "param" };
                p.setProperty ("id",    "mode", nullptr);
                p.setProperty ("value", "III",  nullptr);
                params.addChild (p, -1, nullptr);
            }

            fx.addChild (params, -1, nullptr);
            fxs.addChild (fx, -1, nullptr);
            va.addChild (fxs, -1, nullptr);
        }

        layer.addChild (va, -1, nullptr);

        // layerparams
        {
            juce::ValueTree lp { "layerparams" };
            lp.setProperty ("leveldb",        0.0f,    nullptr);
            lp.setProperty ("pan",            0.0f,    nullptr);
            lp.setProperty ("maincutoffhz",   2000.0f, nullptr);
            lp.setProperty ("mainresonance",  0.2f,    nullptr);
            lp.setProperty ("envamount",      0.5f,    nullptr);
            lp.setProperty ("lforatehz",      1.0f,    nullptr);
            lp.setProperty ("lfodepthsemis",  0.3f,    nullptr);

            juce::ValueTree ampEnv { "ampenv" };
            ampEnv.setProperty ("attackms",  10.0f,  nullptr);
            ampEnv.setProperty ("decayms",   120.0f, nullptr);
            ampEnv.setProperty ("sustain",   0.8f,   nullptr);
            ampEnv.setProperty ("releasems", 600.0f, nullptr);
            lp.addChild (ampEnv, -1, nullptr);

            layer.addChild (lp, -1, nullptr);
        }

        // modulationroutes mínima
        {
            juce::ValueTree routes { "modulationroutes" };

            {
                juce::ValueTree r { "route" };
                r.setProperty ("source",      "LFO1",                  nullptr);
                r.setProperty ("destination", "LayerA.Osc1.pitch",     nullptr);
                r.setProperty ("amount",      0.3f,                    nullptr);
                r.setProperty ("curve",       "sine",                  nullptr);
                r.setProperty ("bipolar",     true,                    nullptr);
                routes.addChild (r, -1, nullptr);
            }
            {
                juce::ValueTree r { "route" };
                r.setProperty ("source",      "ENV1",                  nullptr);
                r.setProperty ("destination", "LayerA.Filter1.cutoff", nullptr);
                r.setProperty ("amount",      0.5f,                    nullptr);
                r.setProperty ("curve",       "exponential",           nullptr);
                r.setProperty ("bipolar",     false,                   nullptr);
                routes.addChild (r, -1, nullptr);
            }

            layer.addChild (routes, -1, nullptr);
        }

        layersVT.addChild (layer, -1, nullptr);
        return presetVT;
    }
}

// ---- TESTS ----

TEST_CASE ("OmegaPreset Juno basic pad roundtrip", "[OmegaPreset][JunoPad]")
{
    // Construir ValueTree de referencia
    auto originalVT = createAceJunoBasicPadValueTree();

    // Crear OmegaPreset desde ValueTree
    auto preset = OmegaPreset::fromValueTree (originalVT);

    SECTION ("Metadata básica")
    {
        REQUIRE (preset.getName()   == juce::String ("ACE Juno Basic Pad"));
        REQUIRE (preset.getEngine() == juce::String ("VirtualAnalog"));
    }

    SECTION ("Layer A estructura mínima")
    {
        auto layers = preset.getLayers();
        REQUIRE (layers.size() == 1);
        const auto& layerA = layers.front();

        REQUIRE (layerA.id   == juce::String ("A"));
        REQUIRE (layerA.name == juce::String ("Juno Basic"));
        REQUIRE (layerA.voiceArch.engine == juce::String ("VirtualAnalog"));
        REQUIRE (layerA.voiceArch.polyphony == 8);

        // Osc1
        REQUIRE (layerA.voiceArch.oscillators.size() == 1);
        const auto& osc1 = layerA.voiceArch.oscillators[0];
        REQUIRE (osc1.componentId == juce::String ("OSC-VA-001"));
        REQUIRE (osc1.enabled == true);
        REQUIRE (osc1.parameters.at ("tune")       == Approx (0.0f));
        REQUIRE (osc1.parameters.at ("pulsewidth") == Approx (0.5f));
        REQUIRE (osc1.parameters.at ("sublevel")   == Approx (0.3f));

        // Flt1
        REQUIRE (layerA.voiceArch.filters.size() == 1);
        const auto& flt1 = layerA.voiceArch.filters[0];
        REQUIRE (flt1.componentId == juce::String ("FLT-VA-001"));
        REQUIRE (flt1.enabled == true);
        REQUIRE (flt1.mode == juce::String ("LP24"));
        REQUIRE (flt1.parameters.at ("cutoff")    == Approx (2000.0f));
        REQUIRE (flt1.parameters.at ("resonance") == Approx (0.2f));
        REQUIRE (flt1.parameters.at ("drive")     == Approx (0.0f));
    }

    SECTION ("Roundtrip toValueTree preserves key fields")
    {
        auto roundVT = preset.toValueTree();

        // Mínimo: nombre, engine y algunos parámetros clave
        REQUIRE (roundVT.getChildWithName ("metadata")
                     .getProperty ("name")
                     .toString()
                     == originalVT.getChildWithName ("metadata")
                                  .getProperty ("name")
                                  .toString());

        REQUIRE (roundVT.getChildWithName ("global")
                     .getProperty ("engine")
                     .toString()
                     == originalVT.getChildWithName ("global")
                                  .getProperty ("engine")
                                  .toString());

        auto origLayerA = originalVT.getChildWithName ("layers").getChild (0);
        auto roundLayerA = roundVT.getChildWithName ("layers").getChild (0);

        REQUIRE (roundLayerA.getProperty ("id").toString()
                 == origLayerA.getProperty ("id").toString());

        auto origVA  = origLayerA.getChildWithName ("voicearchitecture");
        auto roundVA = roundLayerA.getChildWithName ("voicearchitecture");

        auto origOsc = origVA.getChildWithName ("oscillators").getChild (0);
        auto roundOsc = roundVA.getChildWithName ("oscillators").getChild (0);

        REQUIRE (roundOsc.getProperty ("componentid").toString()
                 == origOsc.getProperty ("componentid").toString());
    }
}
Este test asume exactamente la OmegaPreset::Layer, VoiceArchitecture, etc. que definiste; si has cambiado algún nombre de campo, lo ajustamos sobre esto.

